      "node_id": "kg_doc_10",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Tokyo March (東京行進曲 , Tōkyō kōshinkyoku ) is a 1929 black and white Japanese silent film, originally presented with benshi accompaniment, directed by Kenji Mizoguchi. It is a classic melodramatic love tragedy addressing social inequality in modern Japan, depicted in Mizoguchi's typical style. The theme song \"Tokyo March\" was originally sung by Chiyako Sato.",
